            <ArticleTitle>Elevated levels of circulating soluble adhesion molecules in peripheral blood of patients with unstable angina.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>617-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We have demonstrated increased levels of the circulating soluble adhesion molecules (sCAMs), ICAM-1, VCAM-1, and E-selectin in patients with unstable angina compared with healthy controls. Our findings support the role of inflammation in clinically unstable coronary disease, and may indicate a potential role for measurement of peripheral sICAM levels as a marker for inflammatory activity in atherosclerotic plaque.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
